and I don't think any of
my friends would be surprised

1653
01:17:51,390 --> 01:17:52,769
to hear it,
but that's also the way

1654
01:17:52,873 --> 01:17:54,769
that I've chosen
to play this game.

1655
01:17:54,873 --> 01:17:56,459
And it's gotten me a seat
in the final five.

1656
01:17:56,562 --> 01:17:59,735
All I can do
is trust my gut tonight.

1657
01:17:59,838 --> 01:18:02,907
And right now,
I've never felt more confident

1658
01:18:03,011 --> 01:18:05,700
that I'm less confident
in what's going to happen.

1659
01:18:05,804 --> 01:18:08,390
But I'm also sure
that what I do tonight

1660
01:18:08,493 --> 01:18:11,321
will either lose me the game
or possibly win it for me.

1661
01:18:11,424 --> 01:18:13,217
PROBST:
So you're certain

1662
01:18:13,321 --> 01:18:14,873
that you're
completely uncertain?

1663
01:18:14,976 --> 01:18:16,355
Absolutely.

1664
01:18:16,459 --> 01:18:17,735
PROBST:
And you are certain that

1665
01:18:17,838 --> 01:18:19,597
it will either be good or bad?

1666
01:18:19,700 --> 01:18:21,045
You got it.

1667
01:18:21,148 --> 01:18:23,942
Genevieve just spun me
around in circles today,

1668
01:18:24,045 --> 01:18:26,321
like she has many times
in this game

1669
01:18:26,424 --> 01:18:29,148
and I'm sick of it
and I just want

1670
01:18:29,252 --> 01:18:32,286
to survive it one last time,
and that's where I'm at.

1671
01:18:32,390 --> 01:18:34,355
So vote for her.

1672
01:18:34,459 --> 01:18:36,838
I gave the blueprint. I said,
"Genevieve's idol is fake.

1673
01:18:36,942 --> 01:18:39,321
We can all vote for Genevieve."

1674
01:18:39,424 --> 01:18:41,183
And they don't want
to believe it.

1675
01:18:41,286 --> 01:18:42,735
- I don't-I don't really know
what the problem is.
- TEENY: Sam, me

1676
01:18:42,838 --> 01:18:44,252
and you haven't talked. I didn't
say I wasn't voting for her.

1677
01:18:44,355 --> 01:18:45,597
I'm just... Well,

1678
01:18:45,700 --> 01:18:47,459
I'm just saying,
if everybody's got a problem

1679
01:18:47,562 --> 01:18:49,252
with how Genevieve's playing
the game, vote for Genevieve.

1680
01:18:49,355 --> 01:18:51,114
And that's what I've been told
is happening.

1681
01:18:51,217 --> 01:18:52,631
- Everyone's voting for me.
- But it's also hard to trust Sam

1682
01:18:52,735 --> 01:18:54,459
because Sam and Genevieve
work together, and, you know,

1683
01:18:54,562 --> 01:18:57,390
- come up with crazy plans, so...
- RACHEL: I mean, if her idol

1684
01:18:57,493 --> 01:19:00,597
is real, and their two votes
vote out whoever they want,

1685
01:19:00,700 --> 01:19:02,528
- because we all
piled our votes on her.
- Get the picture?

1686
01:19:02,631 --> 01:19:04,562
Yeah.
It's <i>Survivor.</i>

1687
01:19:04,666 --> 01:19:08,286
I am sorry people
don't appreciate the spin

1688
01:19:08,390 --> 01:19:10,252
and they don't appreciate
the stories, but

1689
01:19:10,355 --> 01:19:12,493
what am I supposed to do?
Just go,

1690
01:19:12,597 --> 01:19:14,390
"Okay, game over. You got me"?

1691
01:19:14,493 --> 01:19:15,804
I don't blame you for doing it.

1692
01:19:15,907 --> 01:19:17,804
It's not a lack
of appreciation, Genevieve.

1693
01:19:17,907 --> 01:19:21,252
It's that I also want
to survive in this game.

1694
01:19:21,355 --> 01:19:23,217
And that's my response to it,

1695
01:19:23,321 --> 01:19:26,011
is feeling spun around,
but trying to...

1696
01:19:26,114 --> 01:19:28,286
advocate for myself
and make the best move for me.

1697
01:19:28,390 --> 01:19:29,804
It's not a lack of appreciation.

1698
01:19:29,907 --> 01:19:31,666
- Don't take offense.
- Okay.

1699
01:19:31,769 --> 01:19:34,321
Sam, from the standpoint of

1700
01:19:34,424 --> 01:19:38,045
the five of you looking
to win this season of <i>Survivor,</i>

1701
01:19:38,148 --> 01:19:40,321
is tonight's vote
the biggest vote of the season?

1702
01:19:40,424 --> 01:19:42,011
SAM:
I think they all get bigger.

1703
01:19:42,114 --> 01:19:44,735
The final three is not really,
like, a future plan.

1704
01:19:44,838 --> 01:19:47,942
It's, like, reality
because you're forming it.

1705
01:19:48,045 --> 01:19:49,942
So, yes, each one's bigger

1706
01:19:50,045 --> 01:19:52,045
than the last.

1707
01:19:52,148 --> 01:19:54,183
- Concerning?
- No.

1708
01:19:54,286 --> 01:19:56,493
I'm voting for Genevieve.
Everybody knows.

1709
01:19:59,528 --> 01:20:02,355
PROBST: And, Sue,
you seem very confident.

1710
01:20:02,459 --> 01:20:04,183
You're not concerned
about this conversation, either.

1711
01:20:04,286 --> 01:20:05,942
I... They know where I'm going.

1712
01:20:06,045 --> 01:20:08,459
And I, so far,
have always stuck to my word.

1713
01:20:10,735 --> 01:20:12,011
Are we ready to vote?

1714
01:20:12,114 --> 01:20:13,355
- I'm ready.
- I'm ready.
- I'm ready.

1715
01:20:13,459 --> 01:20:15,390
Are you ready, Teeny?

1716
01:20:15,493 --> 01:20:16,873
Couldn't be more ready.

1717
01:20:16,976 --> 01:20:18,321
I don't know what else
I need to hear.

1718
01:20:22,666 --> 01:20:24,252
All right, it is

1719
01:20:24,355 --> 01:20:27,355
time to vote.
Rachel, you're up.

1720
01:20:41,217 --> 01:20:43,321
♪ ♪

1721
01:20:57,907 --> 01:20:59,390
[sighs]

1722
01:21:12,459 --> 01:21:14,562
♪ ♪

1723
01:21:29,045 --> 01:21:31,080
I'll go tally the votes.

1724
01:21:54,390 --> 01:21:57,045
If anybody has an advantage or
an idol and you want to play it,

1725
01:21:57,148 --> 01:21:59,976
tonight is the last night
you can do so.

1726
01:22:09,011 --> 01:22:10,769
I told you it was fake.

1727
01:22:11,735 --> 01:22:12,769
Aw.

1728
01:22:16,080 --> 01:22:18,045
- All right, I'll read the votes.
- SUE: Jeff?

1729
01:22:18,148 --> 01:22:19,735
I'd like to say something.

1730
01:22:19,838 --> 01:22:22,252
I found this immunity idol

1731
01:22:22,355 --> 01:22:24,976
that I would like
to play tonight for myself.

1732
01:22:25,080 --> 01:22:26,735
[mouths]

1733
01:22:31,528 --> 01:22:33,528
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

1734
01:22:41,080 --> 01:22:43,666
This is a hidden immunity idol.

1735
01:22:43,769 --> 01:22:46,528
Any votes cast
for Sue will not count.

1736
01:22:49,217 --> 01:22:50,873
I'll read the votes.

1737
01:22:53,217 --> 01:22:54,355
First vote:

1738
01:22:54,459 --> 01:22:55,838
Genevieve.

1739
01:22:59,286 --> 01:23:01,804
Sam. That's one vote Genevieve,
one vote Sam.

1740
01:23:06,321 --> 01:23:09,355
Sam. That's two votes Sam,
one vote Genevieve.

1741
01:23:16,045 --> 01:23:17,735
Genevieve.

1742
01:23:17,838 --> 01:23:19,942
We're tied.
Two votes Genevieve,

1743
01:23:20,045 --> 01:23:22,252
two votes Sam, one vote left.

1744
01:23:26,217 --> 01:23:27,838
Fourteenth person voted out

1745
01:23:27,942 --> 01:23:29,735
and the seventh member
of our jury:

1746
01:23:29,838 --> 01:23:31,631
Genevieve.

1747
01:23:31,735 --> 01:23:33,321
Need to bring me your torch.

1748
01:23:34,390 --> 01:23:35,528
SUE:
Good playing, Genevieve.

1749
01:23:35,631 --> 01:23:37,321
- RACHEL: Good game, Genevieve.
- Hugs.

1750
01:23:40,355 --> 01:23:42,390
Come on, give me one.

1751
01:23:47,217 --> 01:23:49,217
Sorry for all the spinning.

1752
01:23:50,321 --> 01:23:51,769
[Teeny mutters]

1753
01:23:59,597 --> 01:24:01,700
Nice.

1754
01:24:15,321 --> 01:24:17,321
Genevieve, the tribe has spoken.

1755
01:24:17,424 --> 01:24:19,321
They have.

1756
01:24:19,424 --> 01:24:20,838
Thank you for the opportunity.

1757
01:24:20,942 --> 01:24:23,045
- I had the time of my life.
- Thanks for being here.

1758
01:24:23,148 --> 01:24:24,528
- Time for you to go.
- TEENY: Bye, Genevieve.

1759
01:24:24,631 --> 01:24:25,976
- Good luck.
- SUE: Bye, Genevieve.

1760
01:24:36,838 --> 01:24:40,148
Congratulations on surviving
another stage of this game.

1761
01:24:40,252 --> 01:24:42,838
You can no longer be voted out.

1762
01:24:42,942 --> 01:24:45,873
Tomorrow you'll compete in
your final immunity challenge.

1763
01:24:45,976 --> 01:24:48,769
The winner earns a spot
in the final three.

1764
01:24:48,873 --> 01:24:51,493
For the other three,
at the very least,

1765
01:24:51,597 --> 01:24:53,700
you'll be making fire,
which means,

1766
01:24:53,804 --> 01:24:57,183
Teeny, Rachel, Sue, Sam,

1767
01:24:57,286 --> 01:24:59,631
any one of you
could win this game.

1768
01:24:59,735 --> 01:25:02,355
Grab your torches.
Head back to camp. Good night.

1769
01:25:03,493 --> 01:25:05,011
Thank you.

1770
01:25:20,045 --> 01:25:22,907
